# What a session keeps safe (E7, E8.7): the join's cookie, content while other machines play it,
# and a client's own character, which only its host can save.
#
# - Every client knocked before its hello and brought back the host's cookie: the host answered
#   knocks, kept nothing of anyone before that, and heard from no game of an older build.
# - Content stays as it is while clients play it: a reload on the host or on a client would desync
#   them, so it is refused, and says when it can be done.
# - c1 saves its character: its game asks the host, which captures the body it plays (the
#   authoritative one) and sends it back; c1 writes it into its slot.
#
# Against a live stand: see coop_smoke.scenario.
stand clients=2 latency=150 loss=0.02
seed 42

# --- setup (dev, on the host): the arena calm, c1's body (e15) healed
@host act npc_set_state id=e6 state=calm
@host act npc_set_state id=e7 state=calm
@host act npc_set_state id=e8 state=calm
@host act npc_set_state id=e14 state=calm
@host act heal id=e15
step 30
invariant !journal "desync"

# --- the join's cookie: knocks answered, nothing dropped for want of a cookie, no older build
@host act net_status
@host expect result contains "\"knocks\":"
@host expect result contains "\"cookieless\": 0"
@host expect result contains "\"older_builds\": 0"

# --- content stays as it is while clients play it
@host act? content_reload
@host expect result contains "refused: a content reload during a co-op session would desync its 2 clients"
@host act? level_reload
@host expect result contains "refused: a level reload during a co-op session"
@c1 act? content_reload
@c1 expect result contains "refused: a content reload during a co-op session would desync this game from its host"

# --- c1 asks the host for its character, and writes what the host sends
mark
@c1 act save_game what=character
@c1 expect result contains "asked of the host"
step 60
@c1 expect journal " saved (save_game, "
@c1 expect !journal "did not send your character"
@host expect journal "net: p1 asked for its character: sent"
